(*MPD:::===================================================================*
 *
 *  Rosetta Project
 *
 *  Module Title     : Windows
 *  Creation date    : 05-SEP-1986
 *  Modification date: 03-DEC-1986
 *  Authors          : Carel Fellinger & Jeroen Medema
 *
 *  Copyright (c) 1986, by Nederlandse Philips Bedrijven BV.
 *
 *  Remarks         : This module defines some basic operations on
 *                    text windows. 
 *
 *                    A text window consists of Characters, lines and
 *                    pages. The reading and writing of Key, Char, Integer,
 *                    Boolean, String and String_String is supported.
 *                    Also some basic window manipulation procedures
 *                    are provided 1) to skip spaces, complete lines and
 *                    pages, 2) to detect end-of-line, end-of-page and
 *                    end-of-window conditions, 3) to end a line or a page,
 *                    4) to reread the last read Character, 5) to determine how
 *                    many Characters have been read/written in the current
 *                    line, 6) to open/close (named) windows, 7) to open/close/
 *                    move viewports, 8) to open/close a device for private
 *                    or shared use and 9) to position the cursor at will.
 *
 *                    The routine ReadAgain makes it easy to implement
 *                    parsers, f.e. if the last read Character was a digit
 *                    then ReadAgain followed by ReadInteger will read and
 *                    convert an Integer, but if it was a letter then ReadAgain
 *                    followed by ReadStr will read the complete String.
 *                    Also end-of-line/end-of-window conditions are detectable
 *                    in a more convinient way.
 *
 *                    The open routines makes it possible to open a window,
 *                    link it to a viewport and link a viewport to a device.
 *                    Moreover it makes it possible to mark the device for
 *                    exclusive or shared use.
 *
 *                    The write functions automatically insert an end-of-line
 *                    in the output Stream if more then MaxIO Characters are
 *                    being written in the current line. This prevents the
 *                    system from breaking down in such a case. The insertion
 *                    is done at the proper places; Strings and Integers are
 *                    never split over two lines, if it does not fit on the
 *                    current line all of it will be written on the next line.
 *
 *                    A call to Windows_Done will return TRUE IFF the last
 *                    Read, Open/Close/Move or Translate action went well. The
 *                    ReadAgain routine has no effect on this.
 *
 *                    Before windows, viewports and devices can be used the
 *                    procedure Windows_Initialize has to be called!
 *
 *                    While performing input the key's <HELP> and <CRTLW> are
 *                    given a special meaning. The first displaying the help
 *                    window; the second to repaint the screen (e.g. after an
 *                    external message).
 *
 *                    Future Extension: Functions to set global variables
 *                    which control the mode of displaying: inserting or
 *                    overwriting.
 *
 *                    16-FEB-1987 Windows_IntegerStatus added for test
 *                     purposes
 *                     Changed the sequence of the parameters in all the
 *                     draw routines to get a uniform interface.
 *                                                       J. Stevens
 *
 *                    16-MAR-1987 x and y in WINDOWS_OpenViewPort exchanged
 *                    in order to let the description be corresponding
 *                    with the actual action.
 *                                                       J. Stevens
 *EMP:::===================================================================*)



(*=========================================================================*
 *  Imported modules
 *=========================================================================*)
pragma C_include('string.pf');
pragma C_include('strings.pf');
pragma C_include('str.pf');


PACKAGE Windows;
WITH strng,str;

